────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PROVENANCE
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

This is an independent implementation of the Clevetura CLVX configuration
protocol, written for interoperability: to let owners of the hardware move
their own settings between their own machines, which the vendor software
provides no way to do.

The wire format was determined by inspecting a device the author owns and by
observing the format used by the vendor's own application, which ships
unminified TypeScript — including its generated protobuf definitions — in the
source maps of its published Electron bundle.

What was taken from that observation is limited to facts about the protocol,
which are not protectable expression and which any correct implementation must
agree on:

  - HID report IDs, packet sizes and the end-of-packet byte
  - the base64 and CRC-32 framing
  - protobuf field numbers and enum values
  - the GATT service and characteristic UUIDs
  - message and field names, field numbers, wire types and enum values for the
    settings tree, taken from those published definitions
  - the units and closed ranges each stored value accepts, and the arithmetic
    relating them to the controls a person sets: that opacity is the complement
    of transparency, that speed and period run the same scale from opposite
    ends, and that a gradient angle is ninety degrees off the stored direction

Those last ones are as much facts about the hardware as the field numbers are:
two correct implementations have no choice but to agree on them, or the device
refuses what they write. They are recorded in docs/PROTOCOL.md §7 so that this
project reads as specification-derived, because it is.

No vendor source code, comments, constant tables, file layout or function
decomposition were copied, and none is redistributed here. Nothing expressive
was taken: the themes, palettes, colour names, window layout, icons and wording
in this project are its own, and were not modelled on the vendor application's.
Every line of this project was written from the protocol description in
docs/PROTOCOL.md.

